<!-- @after 12. Further Reading :: recap -->
### Say these in the interview

- The MediaSessionService creates and releases the player; the UI controls it through a MediaController.
- Track selection follows both playback conditions and user or metered-network constraints.
- PiP changes the UI lifecycle; it is not permission to lose the service-owned playback session.
- For audio-mode task removal, preserve Media3’s default cleanup; deliberately stop video when the product requires it.
- Offline media includes a licence lifecycle and profile boundary, and dataSync foreground-service time limits still apply.
